# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# private/ MUST BE FIRST.
#
# This repository is public and the practice's source material identifies
# thirteen real doctors by name, with sixteen months of their movements.
# private/ holds the project brief, the six research reports, the roster
# images, the diary photograph and the D01..D13 name mapping. None of it is
# ever committed. See docs/DECISIONS.md and the enforcing check in
# scripts/check-no-real-names.mjs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
private/

# Tooling installed into the checkout: gitleaks, uv, Graphify + its interpreter.
# Pinned and checksum-verified by scripts/setup-*.ps1. Never committed.
.tools/

# Graphify. Commit ONLY graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md and manifest.json.
# graph.html is ~600KB of vendored visualisation JavaScript - it is regenerable, it
# bloats every diff, and third-party identifiers inside it trip the real-name check
# (see docs/GRAPHIFY.md). The cache and label sidecars are machine-local.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/graph.json
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md
!graphify-out/manifest.json

# Dependencies
node_modules/
/.pnp
.pnp.*

# Next.js
/.next/
/out/
/build/
next-env.d.ts

# Secrets and local environment
.env*

# Supabase's own CA, downloaded per project (Project Settings -> Database -> SSL Configuration)
# so `db:prod:verify` can do real certificate verification instead of trusting blindly. Not a
# secret, but it is per-environment machine setup, and a stale committed one is worse than none.
*.crt

# Build, test and coverage output
dist/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# Solver (Python) — uv-managed, nothing machine-specific committed
solver/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.ruff_cache/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.pem

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Vercel
.vercel
